# This file describes the SSAPy software citation. The author list is intended
# to reflect software development and stewardship across the inherited internal
# history and the public GitHub repository. It is not derived from a hard
# public commit-count threshold, and squash/merge authorship is not treated as
# original implementation authorship.
#
# SSAPy also has a JOSS paper:
#
# Meyers, J. E., Schneider, M. D., Ebert, J. T., Schlafly, E. F., Yeager, T.,
# Perloff, A., Merl, D., Lifset, N., Bernstein, J., Dawson, W. A., Golovich, N.,
# Higgins, D., McGill, P., Miller, C., & Pruett, K. (2025). SSAPy - Space
# Situational Awareness for Python. Journal of Open Source Software, 10(111),
# 8147. https://doi.org/10.21105/joss.08147
#
# The JOSS paper has its own fixed publication author order. The software
# metadata below reflects repository authorship and maintenance.

